.TH QFW-SLURM-GATEWAY-LAUNCH 8 "September 2026" "qfw-slurm 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
qfw-slurm-gateway-launch \- initialize DEFw and run a gateway command
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qfw-slurm-gateway-launch
.BI --config " path"
.I gateway-command
.RI [ gateway-arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qfw-slurm-gateway-launch
is the supported entry point for gateway commands that contact the DEFw
directory or QPM services. It validates the activated QFw prefix and Python
environment, reads the site directory connection record, prepares the DEFw
parent environment, and replaces itself with
.B defwp
running
.BR qfw-slurm-gateway (8).
.PP
The site systemd unit activates QFw and invokes this command for
.BR serve .
Operators also use it for
.B check
and
.BR retry-release .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --config " path"
Read the gateway YAML configuration and use its QFw activation, virtual
environment, and site configuration paths.
.SH EXAMPLES
Check one registered service:
.PP
.RS
.nf
source /opt/openqse/qfw/bin/qfw-activate \
  --venv /opt/openqse/qfw-venv
qfw-slurm-gateway-launch \
  --config /etc/qfw-slurm/gateway.yaml \
  check --service nwqsim-site
.fi
.RE
.PP
Retry one incomplete release:
.PP
.RS
.nf
qfw-slurm-gateway-launch \
  --config /etc/qfw-slurm/gateway.yaml \
  retry-release 12345
.fi
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QFW_PREFIX
Must identify the activated QFw installation named by the gateway file.
.TP
.B DEFW_PREFIX
Must contain the executable
.IR bin/defwp .
.TP
.B QFW_SHARED_ROOT
Expands the directory connection path selected by the QFw site configuration.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The command exits with the selected gateway command's status. Activation,
configuration, connection-record, or DEFw launcher failures are nonzero.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qfw-slurm-gateway.yaml (5),
.BR qfw-slurm (7),
.BR qfw-slurm-gateway (8)
